skill: Qlik Sense

@ Associative Model | B
What mainly differentiates the Qlik engine from query-based BI tools?
= Its associative model that shows related and unrelated data after every selection
- It stores data only in Excel files
- It does not support visualizations
- It requires SQL for every click
? Qlik keeps all data associated in memory, so selections highlight related values and show excluded ones.

@ Associative Model | A
In Qlik Sense selections, what do the green, white and gray colors mean?
= Selected, associated (possible) and excluded values
- Errors, warnings and success
- Numbers, text and dates
- Primary, foreign and unique keys
? Green values are selected, white values are still possible and gray values are excluded by the current selections.

@ Data Load Script | B
Which file format is Qlik's optimized, fast-loading storage format?
= QVD
- CSV
- XLSX
- JSON
? QVD files are read very quickly and are commonly used for incremental loads and data layers.

@ Data Load Script | I
Which statement loads data from a file or table in the Qlik data load script?
= LOAD
- IMPORT
- READ
- FETCH
? LOAD is the main script statement. SQL SELECT is used to read from databases.

@ Data Load Script | I
What usually causes a synthetic key in a Qlik data model?
= Two tables sharing more than one field with the same name
- A table with no rows
- A field with null values
- Using a QVD file
? Qlik creates a synthetic key to link tables that have multiple fields in common. It is often a sign of a modeling problem.

@ Set Analysis | I
What does Sum({<Year={2024}>} Sales) calculate?
= Total sales for 2024, regardless of the current selection in Year
- Total sales for every year
- The number of sales rows in 2024
- The average sales of 2024
? The set modifier replaces the selection on Year, so the sum covers only 2024.

@ Visualization | B
Which chart is best for comparing values across categories?
= Bar chart
- Gauge
- Map layer
- Text box
? Bar charts make it easy to compare lengths across categories.

@ Visualization | I
What is a master item in Qlik Sense?
= A reusable dimension, measure or visualization defined once and used across sheets
- The first sheet of an app
- A user with administrator rights
- A backup of the data model
? Master items keep definitions consistent and are easy to update in one place.
